0 Fixture: a Z28 gear meshed inside two lap-joined 43038 quarter racks,
0 on a free axle carried by a T-beam. Expected: clean.
0
0 The racks' teeth are a 140-tooth ring, pitch radius 175 (module 2.5
0 LDU, so 1.25 LDU per tooth); the Z28's pitch radius is 35. Meshed, the
0 gear's axle is 175 - 35 = 140 from the ring's centre, which is the
0 racks' origin. MESH asserts exactly that, and excuses the teeth touching
0 with no joint between them -- otherwise CONTACT WITHOUT JOINT.
0
0 MESH does not check the tooth phase. Teeth tip-on-tip interpenetrate,
0 and that is still caught: the gear here is at phase 0, which shares no
0 solid with the racks; turned half a tooth (6.4 degrees) it overlaps.
0
0 46372 is rotates: true, so the gear and its axle reaching the T-beam
0 through one round hole is a bearing, not RIGID CLUSTER HINGE.
0
0 The two T-beams behind tie the 13M beams into one rigid frame: each is
0 pinned twice into the upper beam and once into the lower, the way the
0 half-pipe's posts take two pins each from the motor.
0 !LDRCHECK MESH 46372.dat 24121.dat 140
